❯  === Here's how to use **Mistral AI's OCR model endpoints in Python**:

---

## 🚀 Quick Start

### 1. Install the Python SDK
```bash
pip install mistralai
```

### 2. Set your API key
```bash
export MISTRAL_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
```
*(or set it in your Python code using `os.environ`)*

---

## 📝 Basic Usage

### **Process a PDF or Image from a URL**
```python
import os
from mistralai.client import Mistral

api_key = os.environ["MISTRAL_API_KEY"]
client = Mistral(api_key=api_key)

# Process a PDF
ocr_response = client.ocr.process(
    model="mistral-ocr-latest",
    document={
        "type": "document_url",
        "document_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2201.04234"
    }
)

# Print extracted text from the first page
print(ocr_response.pages[0].markdown)
```

### **Process an Image**
```python
ocr_response = client.ocr.process(
    model="mistral-ocr-latest",
    document={
        "type": "image_url",
        "image_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mistralai/cookbook/main/mistral/ocr/receipt.png"
    }
)
```

---

## ⚙️ Advanced Options

### **Table Formatting**
```python
ocr_response = client.ocr.process(
    model="mistral-ocr-latest",
    document={"type": "document_url", "document_url": "https://example.com/doc.pdf"},
    table_format="html"  # Options: None (default), "markdown", "html"
)
```

### **Extract Headers & Footers**
```python
ocr_response = client.ocr.process(
    model="mistral-ocr-latest",
    document={"type": "document_url", "document_url": "https://example.com/doc.pdf"},
    extract_header=True,
    extract_footer=True
)
```

### **Block Extraction with Bounding Boxes**
```python
ocr_response = client.ocr.process(
    model="mistral-ocr-latest",
    document={"type": "document_url", "document_url": "https://example.com/doc.pdf"},
    include_blocks=True,
    confidence_scores_granularity="block"  # Options: "page", "block", "word"
)
```

### **Confidence Scores**
```python
ocr_response = client.ocr.process(
    model="mistral-ocr-latest",
    document={"type": "document_url", "document_url": "https://example.com/doc.pdf"},
    confidence_scores_granularity="word"  # Per-word confidence scores
)
```

---

## 🔧 Using the REST API Directly

If you prefer raw HTTP requests:

```python
import requests
import json

url = "https://api.mistral.ai/v1/ocr"
headers = {
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    "Authorization": f"Bearer {os.environ['MISTRAL_API_KEY']}"
}

data = {
    "model": "mistral-ocr-latest",
    "document": {
        "type": "document_url",
        "document_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2201.04234"
    }
}

response = requests.post(url, headers=headers, data=json.dumps(data))
result = response.json()
print(result["pages"][0]["markdown"])
```

---

## 📊 Response Structure

The response includes:
- `pages`: List of processed pages
  - `index`: Page number
  - `markdown`: Extracted text in Markdown format
  - `images`: Extracted images (if any)
  - `tables`: Extracted tables (if `table_format` is set)
  - `header`/`footer`: Extracted headers/footers (if enabled)
  - `dimensions`: Page dimensions
  - `confidence_scores`: Confidence metrics (if enabled)
  - `blocks`: Structural blocks with bounding boxes (if enabled)
- `model`: Model used
- `usage_info`: Processing statistics

---

## 💡 Tips

- **Supported formats**: PDF, PNG, JPEG/JPG, AVIF, PPTX, DOCX, and more
- **Multilingual**: Strong performance across 40+ languages
- **Batch processing**: For high-volume workloads, use Mistral's [Batch Inference service](https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/document-processing/overview)
- **Latest model**: Use `mistral-ocr-latest` for the most recent version
- **Python version**: Requires Python 3.10+

---

## 📚 Documentation

- [Official OCR API Reference](https://docs.mistral.ai/api/endpoint/ocr)
- [OCR Processor Documentation](https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/document-processing/basic_ocr)
- [Python SDK Source](https://github.com/mistralai/client-python)

